#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""input — chat REPL, NL shell-command generator, and shell goal-agent for local seats.

Chat REPL:  input [seat|model [base_url]]        thinking streams dimmed
            /models · /system [edit] · /tools · /memory · /location · /think · /clear · /quit
Command:    input -e <task>   propose → execute|revise|describe|copy|quit
            input -x <task>   propose → execute immediately
            input --gen <buf> print one command to stdout (Ctrl-G binding)
Goal agent: input --goal <task>   iterate: propose→confirm→run→observe→next
            input --auto <task>   iterate autonomously; denylist + gemma risk gate
Bare -e/-x/--goal/--auto with no words prompts for the task (no shell quoting).

Seats: gemma (chat default) | coder (command/goal default) | qwen38 (on-demand).
REPL: reasoning streams live then collapses to one line (/think re-expands);
      code blocks stream plain then redraw boxed + line-numbered; ^C copies the last
      reply's code blocks (^D or /quit to exit); /models switches seat. Every request
      is grounded with the current date/time (+ location if /location or settings set).
      A status line under each reply tracks tokens in/out, decode rate, context use, and
      session turns/time.
      Tools: the model can call built-ins (get_current_time; list_files shows an ls -l
      listing; run_command runs shell commands, gated by a gemma risk-review — none/low
      auto-run, riskier prompts; web_search + web_fetch browse the web via Brave) plus
      user tools in ~/.config/input/tools/*.py; /tools
      opens an arrow-key per-tool on/off menu (/tools on|off master switch). Tools from
      MCP servers auto-register DISABLED (enable via /tools); /mcp lists servers (added
      directly vs discovered from ~/.claude.json) and /mcp add <name> <url> adds one.
      Memory: Astoria (the NAS memory service, REST :8933) is wired as an ambient layer —
      relevant memory is recalled before each turn (the server's pre-rendered block) and
      each exchange captured after; /memory toggles/configures (user_id, url in
      settings.json); /memory browse|facts|profile|correct|remember|retract|forget|
      history|as-of|why|health|staging|approve are deterministic REST ops; a built-in
      `memory` tool lets the model persist an explicit correction (the astoria MCP
      server itself stays claimed/hidden while ambient memory is on).
Shell integration (! / !! prefixes, Ctrl-G): source input-shell.bash.
"""
